% ============================================================================
% animal-baby-sex.query.adj — a worked recall over the animal-baby-sex
% library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what is a male baby
% horse called?": it states no fact — it only `import`s the grounded table
% and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `animal_baby_sex` rows and returns the sex-specific name + the table's
% source/locator/trust. An animal/sex pair the source does not distinguish
% abstains honestly — the engine never invents a name.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli animal-baby-sex.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "animal-baby-sex.adj"

? animal_baby_sex(horse, male, $Baby)     % expect colt
? animal_baby_sex(horse, female, $Baby)   % expect filly
? animal_baby_sex(dog, male, $Baby)       % expect abstain — dog has no sex-specific baby name in the source
